Problem: The Windows directoryless workspace fix still relied on dunce::simplified for its lexical containment check. dunce intentionally preserves verbatim UNC paths and paths longer than 260 characters, so a normal network/long base and its persisted verbatim workspace could still be rejected on the next message. Separately, cargo fmt did not traverse agent_local modules declared through include! files.

Objective: Reuse managed directoryless workspaces on local drives, redirected network homes, and long Windows paths without weakening confinement, and ensure future edits to include-hidden Rust sources are format-checked in CI.

Decisions: Keep the allocation-free dunce::simplified/strip_prefix fast path. When the two safe representations still differ, canonicalize both existing paths with std::fs::canonicalize so Windows returns the same verbatim namespace, then derive the relative path from those canonical values. This fallback is fail-closed: I/O failure or a canonical workspace outside the canonical base returns the existing generic workspace error. Existing component validation, symlink rejection, private directory creation, and post-creation canonical containment checks remain unchanged. Preserve dunce::canonicalize at the persistence boundary so ordinary paths continue to be saved in their compatible form.

CI: Add a bounded changed-file format checker for Rust sources under src-tauri/src. It validates the exact base SHA, rejects oversized/traversal/control-character paths, limits Git output and file count, invokes rustfmt through the existing shell-free bounded command runner with a timeout, and emits only a generic failure. The backend CI checkout now fetches the base history required to compare changed files.

Regression coverage: Added Windows cases for normal UNC versus verbatim UNC, local paths over 260 characters, canonical escape rejection, the existing legacy \\?\C: recovery, and the complete directoryless two-resolution flow. The format checker has tests for source scoping, bounded collections, oversized input, traversal rejection, revision validation, and separated rustfmt arguments. Tests were written and observed failing before the implementations.

Self-review: A first green run exposed a regression that returned the legacy verbatim local path; restoring the compatible dunce representation fixed it and the prior test now passes. The final audit also found that the parser needed its own pre-allocation output/path bounds; those were added with failing tests. No provider, Ollama, OAuth, streaming, prompt, prompt-cache, frontend runtime, or user setting code changed.

Validation: cargo test --lib --features windows-tests -- --test-threads=1: 2970 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored. npm test: 412 Vitest files / 1885 tests plus 44 build-script tests, 6 CEF tests, 6 E2E-runner tests, and 51 extension-host tests passed. npm run lint, cargo fmt --check, the changed-source rustfmt check, cargo check --lib --features windows-tests, and cargo clippy --lib --features windows-tests --no-deps -- -A dead-code -D warnings passed. Standard all-target Clippy could not prepare missing CEF because DNS resolution failed; npx tsc --noEmit remains unavailable locally because @wdio/globals/types and mocha type packages are absent. Both are environment limitations unrelated to this diff. graphify update . completed; semantic document update could not run without an LLM API key.
